+# Telegram Admin Manager 0003 — Channel Links and Universal Sorting
+
+## Goal
+Make channel inventory useful for private channels by resolving invite links, and make sorting a consistent persistent behavior in every tabular list in the application.
+
+## Channel links
+- Public channels/groups use `https://t.me/<username>`.
+- Private channels/groups keep a cached invite link in `state.db` when one is available.
+- Full channel inventory may read existing invite links but must not create new links solely as a side effect of scanning.
+- `Обновить ссылки` explicitly refreshes selected/all private channel links. It first tries to reuse an active existing invite created by the current account, then may create a new invite only when that account is owner/admin with `invite_users` capability.
+- No account rotation or repeated retries to bypass Telegram restrictions. FloodWait/restriction handling remains unchanged.
+- When no eligible account can read/create a link, UI displays `Нет доступа к invite-ссылке`; this placeholder is never stored in `link` and is never used as a Telegram target.
+- Cache metadata may include link source session, link refresh timestamp and link status.
+
+## Universal sorting
+- Every `ttk.Treeview` in Telegram Admin Manager and the embedded Twitter/X planner is sortable by clicking a heading.
+- First click sorts ascending; repeated click toggles descending/ascending. Existing live-transfer behavior may keep speed-first-descending where already established, but persisted user choice wins after restart.
+- Each table persists its own sort column and direction.
+- Natural text sort must order `VIP 2` before `VIP 10`.
+- Typed sorting supports numeric, bytes, speed, percent, duration/ETA, date/time and generic text.
+- Dynamic inserts/updates must retain the active sort, not just the initial render.
+- Existing 0001/0002 upload pipeline, account controls, preflight, statistics, channel admin management, FloodWait, Telegram restrictions, FilePartMissing tail requeue, sessions and user data are preserved.
+
+## Version
+- User-visible version: `0003`.
+- Base release: `0002`.
+- Updater manifest compatibility version: `4.3.8.0003`.
